<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lint>
    <!--
      Glance's resource-based ColorProvider(@ColorRes) is annotated
      @RestrictedApi(LIBRARY_GROUP) in the current Glance version, even though
      app code is expected to call it to keep day/night color resources. The
      home-screen widgets use it throughout, which lint flags as RestrictedApi.
      Suppress only that specific false positive (matched on the message) rather
      than disabling the RestrictedApi check or dropping themed color resources.
    -->
    <issue id="RestrictedApi">
        <ignore regexp="ColorProvider can only be called from within the same library group" />
    </issue>

    <!--
      widget_*_preview.xml and glance_default_loading.xml are not app UI. They are
      the static previewLayout/initialLayout thumbnails the launcher renders in the
      widget picker; the live widgets are built with Glance, not by inflating these.
      That makes the layout performance and sizing checks below inapplicable:

        Overdraw                - assumes the layout is inflated into an activity
                                  with Theme.Nimaz. These render in the launcher's
                                  process, with no app theme behind them, so the
                                  root background is the only thing painting.
        SmallSp                 - the previews are drawn at thumbnail scale, where
                                  sub-11sp text is deliberate and never read at 1:1.
        UseCompoundDrawables,
        DisableBaselineAlignment,
        InefficientWeight       - measure/layout micro-optimisations for views that
                                  inflate once in a picker, not in a scrolling app.

      Scoped to those files by name so the same checks still apply to real app
      layouts. RtlSymmetry is deliberately NOT suppressed here - padding symmetry
      is a genuine correctness issue for the app's RTL locales.
    -->
    <issue id="Overdraw">
        <ignore regexp="(widget_.*_preview|glance_default_loading)\.xml" />
    </issue>
    <issue id="SmallSp">
        <ignore regexp="(widget_.*_preview|glance_default_loading)\.xml" />
    </issue>
    <issue id="UseCompoundDrawables">
        <ignore regexp="(widget_.*_preview|glance_default_loading)\.xml" />
    </issue>
    <issue id="DisableBaselineAlignment">
        <ignore regexp="(widget_.*_preview|glance_default_loading)\.xml" />
    </issue>
    <issue id="InefficientWeight">
        <ignore regexp="(widget_.*_preview|glance_default_loading)\.xml" />
    </issue>

    <!--
      Two false positives from the English-centric typo dictionary:

        tr "harf harf" - Turkish reduplication meaning "letter by letter", the
                         intended phrasing for the Qaida subtitle. Not a repeated
                         word by mistake.
        de "in Folge"  - "Tage in Folge" is "days in a row" (the Khatam streak
                         label). Lint suggests "infolge", a different word meaning
                         "as a result of", which would be wrong here.

      Matched on message text so genuine typos elsewhere are still reported.
    -->
    <issue id="Typos">
        <ignore regexp="Repeated word &quot;harf&quot;" />
        <ignore regexp="&quot;in Folge&quot; is a common misspelling" />
    </issue>

    <!--
      REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS is used only to offer an opt-in prompt
      so adhan alarms fire on time; Doze otherwise defers them past the prayer
      time, which defeats the app's core function. This is the exact "alarms and
      reminders that must fire at a precise time" case the Play policy allows, the
      prompt is user-initiated from Home/Onboarding, and the app works (with less
      reliable timing) if the user declines.
    -->
    <issue id="BatteryLife" severity="ignore" />
</lint>
